      <room>H.1302</room>
      <slug></slug>
      <title>Automated Distribution Development and Maintenance</title>
      <subtitle></subtitle>
      <track>CrossDistribution Devroom</track>
      <type></type>
      <language></language>
      <abstract>&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Presenting tools and workflows used via Open Build Service by various distributions to develop the distribution. This includes automated source processing, validation, QA, automated and manual reviews.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Additional focus point on maintenance handling, means updates after a distribution is released which are usually done in a complete different way.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;I like to have a discussion about the question how distributions should validate trustable sources and how the trust can be increased by a common distro effort.&lt;/p&gt;      </abstract>
      <description></description>
      <persons>
          <person id="191">Adrian Schröter</person>
      </persons>
      <links>
          <link href="http://openbuildservice.org/">Open Build Service</link>
      </links>
      <video></video>
      <end></end>
  </event>